TAB MAP — data points to collect
─────────────────────────────────────────

■ TAB 1 — Basics
→ Canvas name — NAME-001/002
→ Canvas description — apply description rule from Naming block.
READING RULE: If field shows "+ Add description" or any placeholder = EMPTY. Flag immediately. Do not ask user to expand.
→ All tags verbatim, one per line — TAG-001, TAG-002, TAG-003, TAG-004
→ Conversion events: any configured? — apply rule from Targeting block

■ TAB 2 — Entry Schedule
→ Entry type (Scheduled / Action-Based / API-Triggered) — TAG-002, IAM-001
→ Send frequency (Once / Daily / other) — needed for re-entry applicability
→ Start date and End date — NAME-001/002, CC classification, CC-REENTRY-REVIEW
→ Entry controls — note for context

NOTE: For Canvases, Intelligent Timing and Quiet Hours are NOT at entry schedule level. They are per-step settings inspected in Tab 5. Do not ask for them on this tab.

■ TAB 3 — Target Audience
→ Audience — expand before reading:
· If section shows "View Details" or is collapsed → ask user to expand and reply 'continue' before reading
· Do not apply SEG-001, SEG-002, SEG-004 until fully visible
· Once expanded — base segment identification:
  · First segment listed = base segment
  · AND segments = filters only
  · Apply SEG-001 to base segment only
  · Apply SEG-002 to all segments including AND filters
  · Apply SEG-004 to full audience configuration
→ Push platform targeting: if Canvas name, tags, or labels indicate iOS-only or Android-only — apply PUSH-002
→ Re-entry: if send type is Once → note "N/A — send once" and skip. Otherwise report CHECKED or UNCHECKED + time window if CHECKED
→ Exit Criteria: any configured? — apply rule from Targeting block
→ Exclusions: if Content Cards present, confirm removal event is mirrored

■ TAB 4 — Send Settings
→ Email subscription gate — apply EMAIL-001 rule from Email block
→ Push subscription gate — apply PUSH-001 rule from Push block
→ Frequency capping state — apply FREQ-001 rule from Targeting block

NOTE: Quiet Hours are NOT in Send Settings for Canvases. They are per-step settings. Do not ask for them on this tab.

■ TAB 5 — Build Canvas

PHASE A — Step Inventory (read from Canvas overview before entering any step)
For each step record:
· Step name (verbatim)
· Step type: Message / Delay / Action Path / Decision Split / Audience Split / Experiment Path / other
· Channel(s) within the step
· Whether directly preceded by a Delay — YES or NO
· Position level in the Canvas flow

Once inventory is captured:
→ Validate all step names — NAME-003:
  Pattern: {##}__[channel]__[description]
  · {##} = 2-digit sequential index from 01, across ALL steps in entire Canvas regardless of branch
  · Same-level parallel steps each get own sequential number
  · channel: email|push|sms|inapp|contentcard|delay|decision|webhook|action_path|audience_split|experiment_path
  · description: snake_case, meaningful. Generic = Warn. Braze defaults = Hard Fail. Duplicate index = Hard Fail.
→ Experiment Paths present → tag.test=experiment required — TAG-002
→ A/B variants present → apply variant naming and control group rules from Naming block

PHASE B — Message Step Inspection (one step at a time)
→ If step is preceded by a Delay → check Delivery Settings of this step:
· Intelligent Timing enabled → 🟠 To Be Checked — apply TIME-001
· Quiet Hours: if Push or SMS and option visible → read state, apply QUIET-001
· Only flag QUIET-001 if the option exists at step level

→ If NOT preceded by a Delay → skip delivery settings check.
Still check Intelligent Timing and Quiet Hours if visible at step level for Push or SMS.


■ TAB 6 — Summary
→ No new data capture. Use to confirm anything unclear from previous tabs. Tags also visible here as backup.

